From d9a9332157b9620613e73a84527b9013828bd1ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: richard-rhino <richard-rhino@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:08:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Spec decode: sampled requests, logprobs and padded batches in
 rejection sampling

The HPU rejection sampler only took greedy requests and asserted otherwise.
It now samples each position from the target distribution, which is rejection
sampling without draft probabilities.

The logits of a decode batch are padded per request, while the sampler indexed
them as compact rows. The sampler now gets metadata in the padded layout, so
sampling constraints, penalties and logprobs read their own rows, and padding
no longer costs a request its bonus token.

The logprobs of speculative steps are returned, with a row per emitted token.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: richard-rhino <richard-rhino@users.noreply.github.com>
